        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "AFAICT, matchit's whole sell is that it provides _vim-specific_ and _regex-based_ matching. Further, given the following parameters:\n\n- we have the opportunity to port this and make it more \"nvim-like\"\n- we'll for sure keep the OG plugin \"around\" - users can opt-in\n\nI see nothing in the discussion so far for why `matchit.lua` can't ***just*** be treesitter. \n\n@ofseed, recall [this comment](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/issues/39683#issuecomment-4408153656).\n\n> since we can define matchit via regex, why not also allow defining matchit using tree-sitter queries?\n\nThis would be nice, but wouldn't it just be a lot simpler and easier to maintain) if we JUST used treesitter?\n\nThis opinion is motivated by #40225 , in which we are (probably) doing in this vein: using treesitter & queries to _vastly_ reduce the code burden of this feature.",
