        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> we need to support...to have _both_ versions of the plugin active at the same time.\n\nCan you please elaborate on this position?\n\nBuiltin plugin migration is confusing but I don't think it should be hard. I'm trying to think of a way forward here, but I cannot see any reconcilable way to have matchit & ts matching available on the same buffer. The only tenable idea I see is having non-ts langs have a vim plugin fallback--and even this is borderline confusing.\n\nThe migration process is a grey area (to me, at least). I don't even see why we need to keep these two plugins (matchit, matchparen) SEPARATE in the corresponding nvim impl. At this point, I'm leaning towards a single \"match.lua\" (or something of the sort) that combines matchparen & matchit (where we only match pairs & use ts queries, no `match_words`), being entirely disjoint from the vim counterparts.\n\nJust trying to find a way forward here 8) ",
