        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "> At least one of our goals is to make matchit.vim work together with matchparen, so that the behavior becomes effectively WYSIWYG: matchit should jump to the position currently highlighted by matchparen. Therefore, we would need to trigger the search after a CursorMoved event, while pressing % should make matchit jump directly to a position that has already been computed.\n\nRegarding highlights, I like matchit.vim's current behavior of _not_ highlighting `b:match_words` groups, but still enhancing `%` on those. On the other side, I like matchparen's current behavior of highlighting `'matchpairs'` (`hl-MatchParen`).\n\nFrom what I understand, the WYSIWYG target being discussed in this thread is scoped to matchparen's current scope, i.e., single-char pairs, excluding matchit.vim's groups (string groups). So the Lua port will _not_ highlight the latter matches, keeping current highlighting behavior.\n\nI appreciate this highlithing asymmetry as highlighting only single-char pairs reduces visual noise while preserving the functionality to `%` between `function`/`end` and alike. However, there seems to also be interest in having matchit.vim highlight: https://github.com/chrisbra/matchit/issues/45\n\nAll this just to say that I would appreciate keeping highlighting separate on the Lua port, so I can disable it for the string groups (if a highlight groups is introduced for this) and keep highlighting only enabled for the single-char pairs.",
